Description: hw/misc: Add the i.MX21 PWM
 The Chumby's stock kernel drives the LCD backlight with the PWM (TOUT2
 on PE5) in its sense1 driver: it resets the block through PWMC's SWR
 bit and waits for the bit to clear, sets the period to 0xfffc, then
 on every jiffy writes the level (700 to 0xffff) to PWMS, checking
 PWMC's FIFO-available bit first, and enables the block with
 PWMC = 0x10. A level of 0xffff, beyond the period, keeps the backlight
 fully on.
 .
 Model a period of PWMP + 2 counter cycles, clocked from PERCLK1 through
 the prescaler and CLKSEL or from the 32 kHz clock; samples queue in a
 FIFO (two deep, a guess: the manual's depth is not to hand) that FIFOAV
 reports, and each takes over at the end of a period for REPEAT periods;
 the counter register counts; SWR resets the block at once, so it never
 reads as set.
 .
 The output is a GPIO output line whose level is the duty cycle, 0 to
 0xffff, so a board can show it. It changes only when the guest changes
 the duty cycle, not at reset, so the board decides what an unprogrammed
 PWM shows. The interrupt and the audio byte swaps are not modelled.
Author: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
